    <!-- MailAccountScreens.kt · support -->
    <string name="mail_support_i_forgot_my_password">I forgot my password. What now?</string>
    <string name="mail_support_tap_forgot_password_sign">Tap Forgot password on the sign-in screen. GrapMail emails a reset link to the recovery email on your account, so add and verify one in Personal info before you need it.</string>
    <string name="mail_support_can_i_sign_my">Can I sign in with my phone number?</string>
    <string name="mail_support_yes_sign_page_accepts">Yes. The sign-in page accepts either the GrapMail address or the phone number you verified, but the number is never the identity of the account, and mail is never addressed to it.</string>
    <string name="mail_support_i_changed_my_number">I changed my number. Will I lose the account?</string>
    <string name="mail_support_no_if_change_before">No, if you change it before losing access. The new number is proven with a code before it replaces the old one.</string>
    <string name="mail_support_why_can_i_not">Why can I not create an account for someone under 13?</string>
    <string name="mail_support_grapmail_holds_address_can">GrapMail holds an address that can receive mail from anyone, so the account requires an age of at least 13. The birthday you enter is checked against that rule.</string>
    <string name="mail_support_what_alias">What is an alias for?</string>
    <string name="mail_support_alias_delivers_into_same">An alias delivers into the same mailbox under a second address, and can be chosen as the sender. Useful when you want to write as “business” without a second account.</string>
    <string name="mail_support_mail_i_was_expecting">Mail I was expecting never arrived.</string>
    <string name="mail_support_order_check_sending_address">In order: check the sending address was spelled exactly, look in Spam and Trash under “Others”, then check that the sender is not on the suppression list because they unsubscribed earlier. If the mailbox is connected and the message is still missing, the mail server has to be involved. That is a support matter.</string>
